     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>Le lundi 30 novembre 2015 18:22:42 UTC+1, Joe Cheng [RStudio] a écrit :<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Ah, we already had an issue for this:<div><a href=\"https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/692\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/692&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792395861684000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Mm0CR_-nZdWED8ohrmSjD\">https://github.com/rstudio/shiny/issues/692</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ll see if I can figure out a fix.</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Nov 30, 2015 at 9:21 AM Joe Cheng &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">j...@rstudio.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">There seems to be a bug. You can work around it for now by putting withMathJax around uiOutput(&quot;regression&quot;) as well.</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Nov 30, 2015 at 7:06 AM Paul Deveau &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">deveau.p...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<br><br>I am quite new with Shiny, but I stumbled onto a conflict between withMathJax and slider creations in the same renderUI.<br>Using the p function instead of withMathJax can overcome the issue, but it will not compile the LaTeX code.<br><br>I put below a minimal code for a reproducible example:<br><br>In the server.R:<br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#6